We want to find the probability that we get heads in at least 9 of the 11 flips, which is $P(X \ge 9)$. This is equal to $P(X=9) + P(equiv{10}) + P(X=11) + P(X=12)$.
The probability of getting exactly $k$ heads in $n$ flips is given by the binomial probability formula:
$$P(X=k) = \binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}$$
In this case, $n=12$ and $p=05$, so
$$P(X=k) = \binom{12}{k} (0.5)^k (0.5)^{12-k} = \binom{12}{k} (0.5)^{12}$$
We want to find $P(X \geq 9) = P(X=9) + P(X=10) + P(X=11) + P(X=12)$.
