$$y - f(a) = f'(a)(x - a)$$

This is the equation of the tangent line to the graph of $f$ at the point $(a, f(a))$.

We can rewrite this equation in slope-intercept form form:
$$y = f'(a)(x - a) + f(a)$$
$$y = f'(a)x - a f'(a) + f(a)$$

